// A PREDICATE IS NOT A SORT.
//
// `pred`/`func` declare CALLABLES, which have signatures, not sorts. `marks(x)` is a
// proposition and `marks` itself has no sort at all — so it cannot be a binder's sort. (Same
// for a `func`: see `sorts_reject_func_as_sort.b4m`.)
//
// This has always been rejected in binder position by `resolveSortTok`'s kind check; the
// fixture pins it, because the Prop demotion reworked that function and the SCHEMA-PARAMETER
// position still accepts a callable name silently until something instantiates the schema.
sort Elem
pred marks(x: Elem)

theorem aPredIsNotASort: forall p: marks; p = p
proof
  @conclusion |
    forall p: marks; p = p
    [by reflexivity]
qed
